=== P3 Dashboard widget 0097 SubscriptionsWidget (Android) ===
Capability: Jetpack Compose + Material 3, Kotlin (repo pins 2.x; prompt floor 2.2.x) -- AVAILABLE
  (JDK 21 JetBrains JBR at %JAVA_HOME%, Android SDK at %LOCALAPPDATA%\Android\Sdk, gradlew 8.14.5).
  :android:assembleRelease produces a Release APK (gate below), so the platform capability is present --
  this gate is NOT a platform-capability block. NOTE: the Gradle module path is ':android' (settings.gradle.kts
  include(":android"); projectDir = app/), so the prompt gate's ':app:'/'ktlintCheck'/'detekt' are addressed as
  ':android:assembleRelease', ':android:testReleaseUnitTest', ':android:ktlintCheck', ':android:detekt'. The
  unit-test scope is artifact-isolated to '*subscriptions*' (the shared androidTest source set is not host-run;
  no emulator), matching the P3/0047 EnergySiteInfo precedent.

P3 core prerequisites reused: A1 theme/tokens (TeslaTokens/Spacing), shared component library
  (ui: GlassPanel/Icon/IconButton/Badge/PanelTitle/Caption/BodyText/MetricValue/MetricLabel; feedback:
  EmptyState/ErrorDisplay/Skeleton/FeedbackGlyphs; datadisplay: DataFreshness), S7/S8 vehicles data layer
  (VehiclesRepository / VehiclesStore -> vehicles + vehicleSubscriptions), S10 i18n catalog, S11 diagnostics
  Logger (view.opened), S8 BaseFeedViewModel/UiState/Resource cache-then-network contract.

Web source: web/src/features/dashboard/widgets/SubscriptionsWidget.tsx (THE spec). Native output:
  apps/android/app/src/main/java/com/teslasync/dashboard-widgets/SubscriptionsWidget/
    SubscriptionsModel.kt            (pure parse + daysUntil + projection + registration; no Compose/Android/HTTP)
    SubscriptionsSource.kt           (data port + S7 VehiclesRepository / S8 VehiclesStore adapters)
    SubscriptionsWidgetViewModel.kt  (resolves first vehicle -> vehicleSubscriptions onto UiState)
    SubscriptionsWidget.kt           (Compose: WidgetShell-equiv header + compact hero + standard detail list)
Tests: src/test/.../subscriptions/{SubscriptionsProjectionTest(19), SubscriptionsWidgetViewModelTest(11)};
       src/androidTest/.../subscriptions/SubscriptionsWidgetUiTest(7).

Parity (web -> native):
  - Registry: id 'subscriptions', category 'vehicle', default 2x4, min 1x2, max 4x40 (SubscriptionsRegistration).
  - States: loading skeleton; hard error + retry (ONLY when the per-vehicle subscriptions feed errors w/ no
    cache, web isError from useVehicleSubscriptions); content; empty (web parseSubscriptions==[] => EmptyState,
    "No subscriptions"); stale/offline cached + freshness chip; a vehicles-list error degrades to a cached empty
    (web disables the subscriptions query when no id resolves, so it never raises the error surface).
  - Compact (size.cols<=1): CreditCard glyph + active count + "active" label + soonest-expiry chip, else empty.
  - Standard (>1 col): title "Subscriptions" + CreditCard icon; one row per subscription (name; formatted expiry
    MMM d, yyyy else renewal else em-dash; Active/Expired badge). Known SUBSCRIPTION_TYPES then generic array,
    de-duplicated case-insensitively by name (web parseSubscriptions).
  - daysUntil = Math.ceil((expiry-now)/86400000); asString / Boolean(val) coercions reproduced.
  - i18n: 6 chrome keys resolve from S10 (translation_widget_subscriptions_{title,active,expired,activeCount,
    noData,unknown}); the 6 SUBSCRIPTION_TYPES labels resolve via key+fallback (web t(labelKey, fallback)) using
    a runtime resource lookup -- the catalog ships these as fallback-only, identical to web, so no catalog edit.
  - a11y: refresh IconButton labelled; each detail row + the compact hero fold into one TalkBack phrase.
  - Telemetry: view.opened emitted once with surface slug 'SubscriptionsWidget' (P1/S11).

